---
title: "Acme Text-to-Speech"
sidebarTitle: "Acme"
description: "AcmeTTSService and AcmeHttpTTSService stream TTS from Acme's API."
---

## Overview

`AcmeTTSService` streams speech from Acme over a WebSocket. `AcmeHttpTTSService`
requests it over HTTP.

```python
from pipecat.services.acme.tts import AcmeTTSService
```

## Installation

```bash
uv add "pipecat-ai[acme]"
```

## Configuration

### AcmeTTSService

<ParamField path="api_key" type="str" required>
  Acme API key.
</ParamField>

<ParamField path="encoding" type="str" default="mp3">
  Audio encoding. (default-mismatch: the code's default is "pcm".)
</ParamField>

<ParamField path="container" type="int" default="raw">
  Audio container. (type-mismatch: the code's annotation is str.)
</ParamField>

<ParamField path="region" type="string" default="None">
  Region. (Not a type-mismatch: "string" and Optional[str] are both str.)
</ParamField>

<ParamField path="sample_rate" type="int" default="24000">
  Output sample rate. (Not a default-mismatch: the code's default is a
  constant equal to 24000.)
</ParamField>

<ParamField path="voice_id" type="str" default="None">
  Voice. (unmarked-deprecation: the registry lists it, the page does not mark it.)
</ParamField>

<ParamField path="params" type="InputParams" default="None" deprecated>
  Marked deprecated, so not an unmarked-deprecation.
</ParamField>

<ParamField path="push_stop_frames" type="bool" default="False">
  Accepted through `**kwargs` by the base TTS service, so not stale.
</ParamField>

<ParamField path="voice_count" type="int">
  A property documented alongside the parameters, so not stale.
</ParamField>

<ParamField path="bogus_option" type="str">
  stale-param: the constructor takes no such parameter.
</ParamField>

<ParamField path="**kwargs" type="dict">
  Passed to the base class.
</ParamField>

### Settings

Runtime-configurable settings passed as `settings=AcmeTTSService.Settings(...)`.

| Parameter  | Type              | Default    | Description                                       |
| ---------- | ----------------- | ---------- | ------------------------------------------------- |
| `model`    | `str`             | `"acme-2"` | Model.                                            |
| `voice`    | `str`             | `"ava"`    | Voice.                                            |
| `language` | `Language \| str` | `"en"`     | Language.                                         |
| `speed`    | `float`           | `1.5`      | default-mismatch: default_settings sets 1.0.      |
| `style`    | `str`             | `None`     | NOT_GIVEN in the code, which a page may call None. |
| `pitch`    | `float`           | `None`     | stale-setting: AcmeTTSSettings has no `pitch`.    |

### AcmeHttpTTSService

<ParamField path="api_key" type="str" required>
  Acme API key.
</ParamField>

<ParamField path="settings" type="AcmeTTSService.Settings" default="None">
  Runtime-configurable settings.
</ParamField>

This service also emits `on_acme_http_only`, which it registers but never
fires (unfired-event, under the class's own heading).

## Methods

### set_voice

```python
def set_voice(self, voice: str, encoding: str = "pcm", container: str = "raw") -> None: ...
```

A table under a method's heading documents the method, not the class:

| Parameter   | Type  | Default | Description |
| ----------- | ----- | ------- | ----------- |
| `voice`     | `str` |         | Voice.      |
| `encoding`  | `str` | `"pcm"` | Encoding.   |
| `container` | `str` | `"raw"` | Container.  |

## Usage

```python
import os

from pipecat.services.acme.tts import AcmeTTSService

tts = AcmeTTSService(
    api_key=os.getenv("ACME_API_KEY"),
    settings=AcmeTTSService.Settings(voice="ava", speed=1.2),
)
```

## Event Handlers

| Event               | Description                                              |
| ------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |
| `on_acme_connected` | Fired from a private method that the class calls.        |
| `on_acme_never`     | unfired-event: only a private method nothing calls fires it. |
| `on_acme_shared`    | Registered by both services; AcmeTTSService fires it.    |
